EXT. CABLE CAR GONDOLA, MIDWAY OVER ALPINE GORGE - NIGHT

A tiny glass cabin dangling from a single cable above a black abyss. Wind groans through the steel. Snow beads on the windows. Inside, four passengers sit pressed together on cold benches, lit by a flickering emergency strip.

MAGNUS HALVORSEN, fifties, a ski instructor in a red parka, grips the safety rail. SOLEDAD "SOL" ARRIAGA, thirties, a nurse in a cardigan, kneels beside the seat where PRISCILLA TRENT, seventies, in a fur-trimmed coat, sits very pale. JIN-HO PARK, twenties, a backpacker, holds a dead phone in both hands.

MAGNUS
Stay calm. They'll restart the motor in the next few minutes.

SOL
You said that twenty minutes ago, Magnus.

MAGNUS
And I'll say it again.

JIN-HO
Is it moving?

PRISCILLA
Everything's moving, dear. We're on a string.

SOL
Mrs. Trent, look at me. Breathe through your nose.

PRISCILLA
I am breathing, Soledad.

SOL
Slower, then.

The gondola lurches. Everyone grabs something. Jin-ho slides across the bench into Magnus, and Magnus catches him by the front of his jacket.

JIN-HO
Sorry, sorry --

MAGNUS
Sit. Hold the bar.

A sharp metallic crack from the cable above. The cabin drops three feet, swings, and slams to a halt. Priscilla cries out. Sol throws her arms around her. Magnus and Jin-ho fall together against the glass and for a moment all four are a heap of coats, elbows, gasps.

MAGNUS (CONT'D)
Everyone, don't move!

No one does. The cabin sways, slowly, like a pendulum losing its argument.

SOL
(whispering)
Jin-ho, can you reach the hatch?

JIN-HO
It's over my head.

SOL
Magnus can lift you.

MAGNUS
Not with this rope between my --

PRISCILLA
Magnus Halvorsen, you will lift that boy.

A beat. Magnus nods. He braces his boots against the bench and cups his hands. Jin-ho steps up, one knee on Magnus's palms, and fumbles at the roof hatch. It resists. He pounds it with his fist, and it pops open, and a rope ladder tumbles down into the cabin from a rescue helicopter's lamp, white and blinding.

SOL
(laughing, sobbing)
Priscilla! Priscilla, look!

PRISCILLA
I see it, dear. I'm not blind.

Magnus bursts into tears.
